# Native JioSaavn provider

This Kotlin implementation ports the catalog, identity, media decoding and quality behavior in `../jiosaavn`. It implements `dev.metrofuse.api.NativePlugin` directly and uses the host's isolated, asynchronous HTTP client and persisted settings. DES locator decoding uses JVM `javax.crypto`; no JavaScript engine or bundled copies of host libraries are needed.

Catalog mapping, DES key and catalog-region headers originate in the user-supplied Metrolist Project (C) 2026, GPL-3.0 `JioSaavnAudioProvider.kt`, recorded in `../jiosaavn/SOURCE`. Preserve this attribution and the bundled GPL license. The regional catalog setting restores the upstream API request routing for Western-label releases. Routing headers are never attached to CDN streams; the plugin supplies no authentication sessions or DRM support.

Build with `gradlew.bat :plugin-jiosaavn-native:packagePluginJar :plugin-jiosaavn-native:packagePluginApk`. Outputs are `build/plugin-examples/jiosaavn.jar` for desktop and `build/plugin-examples/jiosaavn.apk` for Android. Both compile the same Kotlin implementation. The JAR contains compiled JVM classes and a root native manifest; the APK contains D8-compiled DEX, an Android resource manifest and `assets/metrofuse/manifest.json`. Host libraries are compile-only and are not bundled in either artifact. Both include source attribution and the GPL license.

Import through Settings → Plugins on the appropriate platform. The APK is a dynamically imported provider container, with no standalone launcher application. It uses the same plugin ID and settings as `jiosaavn.mfp`, so importing the other format replaces the installed implementation. The MFP remains the cross-platform artifact for Android and desktop. Android minimum API is 24: Base64 decoding is platform-neutral, and URL escaping uses the String charset-name overload available on older Android releases. No JNI libraries are bundled.

The initial Android device import test reported a missing native manifest. Windows AAPT2 used a backslash in `assets/metrofuse\manifest.json`; Python ZIP inspection normalized it, while Java/Android ZIP lookup did not. The APK packer now normalizes every archive path to forward slashes using the same convention as the native examples. It writes standard Java ZIP entries, with no directory entries, stored Android resources and four-byte APK alignment. Device checks for the revised APK are left to the user. The Android compatibility changes passed the existing deterministic native provider tests. No successful Android playback result is claimed for this APK revision.

On 14 November 2026, deterministic routing/cache, decoder/quality and partial-search tests passed. The production engine loaded the actual JAR with shared host API identity and passed repeated activation, disable, reload and restart persistence. The opt-in Western catalog test found and resolved six originals by Don Toliver, The Weeknd and Travis Scott at 320 kbps, with metadata, album membership and CDN MP4 signatures checked. FFprobe identified AAC and FFmpeg decoded three seconds for each JAR stream, as well as all six MFP counterparts. Reports are under `build/jiosaavn-western-live/`; these are desktop runtime and decoder checks, not application UI or Android playback tests.
